le integrals of the signed normalized longitudinal Gram error at all actual waist stations, evaluated by cyclic trapezoid weights on the actual angular labels. The constant plus first, second and third cosine/sine rows enter the nonlinear loss, its true physical Jacobian and the signed compressive second variation. Each independent check records each mode maximum and its real station. Whole relative Gram, signed near-normal pairs, distant material chord, curvature, area and all cap/transition charts remain present.","The working physical displacement is linear in its new coefficients after the finite named field is formed. Complete top-point Gram and all added moment stresses are included in a deterministic full-time Ritz model. Auxiliary nonsmooth constraint Hessians are omitted, and both candidate signs are judged by the original nonlinear full objective and true physical position/tangent trust restrictions.","All 3 families retain a certified actual material terminal witness and a pointwise fixed right strip. This does not certify embeddedness, the quotient distance or reach after free corrections. Fixed normal cost uses a stronger initial-diameter upper-bound target, while the intrinsic far-material row is necessary for the actual reach requirement. Samples and original analytic facts are distinguished throughout.","The initial metric already has positive and negative Gauss curvature cells on the actual bent shoulder. A smaller held field, a rigid far head, finite closed sampling or the absence of numerical intersections alone do not solve the full metric condition. Each full NPZ and PLY stays on the defining runner."],"schema":"r791-prebent-waist-gram-moment-stress-run-v1","sources":{"bent_prebent_waist_fields.py":"6e825f59a1ec0ee9a4a181a0de584ff1c6d5bf7a3640444dfd6d65da5db93a1e","bent_prebent_waist_normal.py":"a2f14d9b52cc42877cff8223350075dc457869472acd3f053861c54efa35a2f5","bent_prebent_waist_phase.py":"56f524b63f6799db75aae54c143c019c8d2c72acf82b78e9db9431f